<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Émile Ollivier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1825">1825</a>–<a href="/years/1913">1913</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Emile Ollivier</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Émile Ollivier was a French liberal politician who rallied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a> and in January 1870 became head of government of the parliamentary 'Liberal Empire'. His ministry was approved by a plebiscite in May 1870, but he led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a> that July, and he fell from office after the first defeats in August.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emile-ollivier.jpg" alt="Émile Ollivier" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pierre-Louis Pierson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%89mile_Ollivier_by_Pierre-Louis_Pierson,_1870.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
